# park-cascade-demo.msh -- a real show excerpt from EMLG000E, redacted to
# the countdown-cascade changes of state only (11 beats instead of ~160 raw
# frames). Generated by tools/gen_show_script.py then hand-trimmed: the
# timeline is renormalised so the fade starts at @0, and the genuine ~27 s
# capture gap after the fade (only idle pings + broadcasts) is compressed
# to ~3 s so the demo gets moving -- the strobe-ramp pacing inside the
# excerpt is preserved exactly.
#
# Each `cascade hex <delay-led phrase>` line expands to a sparse countdown
# chain: one member every --cascade-ms (default 400 ms: FD F9 F5 F1 then
# the 20 immediate go copy) -- every member collapses the audience onto the
# same beat, so a handful of sends replaces the 14-member capture broadcast
# (--cascade-full restores that). Edit any phrase or @ms freely; this is
# the script.
#
# Dry-run the plan:   mwm-send.py --dry-run sequence samples/park-cascade-demo.msh
# The plan reads as a lookahead cue sheet: each row is ONE master event,
# classified (PRE_BUFFER_EVENT etc.) with its `master-beat` collapse marker.
# Send it:            mwm-send.py sequence samples/park-cascade-demo.msh

# --- The fade-to-black cascade (soft) -------------
@0
cascade hex F1 48 85 58 64
  # both ears fade out, cycle timer 0x64 (~100 ms/count)

# --- Strobe stand; timer ramps 0x19..0x02 over four beats ---
@3000
cascade hex F1 24 67 58 19 48 84
  # strobe into running program, timer 0x19 (was @139086)
@6200
cascade hex F1 24 67 58 0F 48 84
  # strobe, timer 0x0F
@8200
cascade hex F1 24 67 58 07 48 84
  # strobe, timer 0x07
@11134
hex 96FD24675802488488
  # strobe, timer 0x02; captured GO member (single, non-cascade)